{"qid":"Q157070","names":["County of Flanders"],"title":"County of Flanders","endonym":{"native":"Comté de Flandre","lang":"fr"},"capsule":"The County of Flanders was established in 862 when Charles the Bald appointed Baldwin I 'Iron Arm' as first count to defend the Flemish coast against Norse raids, and it grew into one of the most economically powerful principalities of medieval Europe. Its wealth rested on the textile industry — Ghent, Bruges, and Ypres were among the busiest cloth-producing cities in northern Europe — and on control of the Scheldt estuary trade. The county's conflicts with the French Crown culminated in the Battle of the Golden Spurs (1302), where a Flemish communal militia defeated the French cavalry. After the extinction of the male line, it passed by marriage to the Dukes of Burgundy in 1384 and was incorporated into the Habsburg Netherlands by 1477.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The county's core territory is well attested through charters, feudal surveys, and administrative records; frontier zones with Artois and Hainaut shifted through diplomacy and war but are broadly reconstructable from medieval documents.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: County of Flanders","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/County_of_Flanders"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Baldwin I, Count of Flanders","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baldwin_I,_Count_of_Flanders"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Battle of the Golden Spurs","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Golden_Spurs"}],"britannica":"place/Flanders-medieval-principality-and-historical-region-Europe","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Cou